@startuml cls-biometric
title Class Diagram — Biometric

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class Person <<external — identity>> {
}
class AppUser <<external — identity>> {
}

enum BiometricType <<enumeration>> {
  FACIAL
  FINGERPRINT
}

enum UpdateStatus <<enumeration>> {
  Pending
  In_Review
  Approved
  Rejected
}

class BiometricUpdateCase {
  +caseId: UUID
  +personId: UUID
  +biometricType: BiometricType
  +fingerNumber: Int
  +currentEmbeddingRef: String
  +reason: String
  +updateStatus: UpdateStatus
  +requestedBy: UUID
  +requestedAt: DateTime
  +reviewedBy: UUID
  +reviewedAt: DateTime
  +resolutionNotes: String
  +request()
  +review(decision)
}

class FacialEmbedding <<MongoDB document>> {
  +_id: ObjectId
  +personId: UUID
  +templateVersion: Int
  +encoding: Float[]
  +modelVersion: String
  +enrolledAt: DateTime
  +isActive: Boolean
  +enroll()
  +deactivate()
}

class FingerprintEmbedding <<MongoDB document>> {
  +_id: ObjectId
  +personId: UUID
  +fingerNumber: Int
  +templateVersion: Int
  +encoding: Float[]
  +modelVersion: String
  +enrolledAt: DateTime
  +isActive: Boolean
  +enroll()
  +deactivate()
}

BiometricUpdateCase --> BiometricType
BiometricUpdateCase --> UpdateStatus

BiometricUpdateCase ..> Person : person_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
BiometricUpdateCase ..> AppUser : requested_by / reviewed_by\n(cross-context, no FK)
BiometricUpdateCase ..> FacialEmbedding : current_embedding_ref\n(cross-paradigm Mongo _id, no FK)
BiometricUpdateCase ..> FingerprintEmbedding : current_embedding_ref\n(cross-paradigm Mongo _id, no FK)
FacialEmbedding ..> Person : person_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
FingerprintEmbedding ..> Person : person_id\n(cross-context, no FK)

note left of BiometricUpdateCase
  Logically owned by Biometric, physically
  hosted in the configuration schema (transient,
  see AGENTS.md §4.6). chk_finger_number: 1..10
  only if biometricType=FINGERPRINT, else NULL.
  requestedBy/requestedAt are mandatory. This is
  the canonical shape exposed at
  ms-configuration /api/v1/biometric-update-cases
  (Postgres) — ms-biometric also runs its own
  independent MongoDB implementation of the same
  feature at /api/v1/biometric/update-request*
  with no requestedBy, no fingerNumber check, and
  no sync to this one. See SEQ-04 and
  c4-biometric-service.mmd.
end note

note right of FacialEmbedding
  RN-28: only one active embedding per person
  at a time (isActive flag) — enroll()
  deactivates the previous template.
end note

note right of FingerprintEmbedding
  RN-27: supports up to 10 fingers per person,
  one active template per finger.
end note

note as N1
  FacialEmbedding/FingerprintEmbedding have no
  audit block (MongoDB documents, not SQL rows —
  see AGENTS.md §4.6). BiometricUpdateCase does
  carry the standard SQL audit block
  (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/
  updated_by/deleted_by/row_version), omitted
  here for readability. See
  06-data/domains/06-biometric.md and
  08-configuration.md for the column-level view
  (06-biometric.md has no erDiagram of its own —
  see the note in diagram-index.md).
end note

@enduml
